 880:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     ****************************************************************************//**
 881:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * \brief
 882:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * Selects the WCO block output source.
 883:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     *
 884:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * In addition to generating 32.768 kHz clock from external crystals, WCO 
 885:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * can be sourced by external clock source using wco_out pin. The API help to
 886:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * lets you select between the sources: External crystal or external pin.
 887:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     *
 888:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * If you want to use external pin to drive WCO the next procedure is required:
 889:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 1) Disable the WCO.
 890:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 2) Drive the wco_out pin to an external signal source.
 891:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 3) Call CySysClkWcoClockOutSelect(CY_SYS_CLK_WCO_SEL_PIN).
 892:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 4) Enable the WCO and wait for 15 us before clocking the XO pad at the high 
 893:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * potential. Let's assume you are using the 1.6v clock amplitude, then the
 894:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * sequence would start at 1.6v, then 0v, then 1.6v etc at a chosen frequency.
 895:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     *
 896:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * If you want to use WCO after using an external pin source:
 897:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 1) Disable the WCO.
 898:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 2) Drive off wco_out pin with external signal source.
 899:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 3) Call CySysClkWcoClockOutSelect(CY_SYS_CLK_WCO_SEL_CRYSTAL).
 900:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * <br> 4) Enable the WCO.
 901:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     *
 902:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * \warning 
 903:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * Do not use the oscillator output clock prior to a 15uS delay in your system.
 904:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * There are no limitations on the external clock frequency.
 905:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * \warning 
 906:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * When external clock source was selected to drive WCO block the IMO can be 
 907:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * trimmed only when external clock source period is equal to WCO external
 908:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * crystal period. Also external clock source accuracy should be higher 
 909:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     * or equal to WCO external crystal accuracy.
 910:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO2.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\CyLFClk.c ****     *
